From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Unlock the frame rate while the render thread draws

In game Halo 3 draws on its RENDER thread: the main thread simulates and
publishes a copy of the frame to a queue, and the mode word 82948F68 is 1.
The unlock was gated on that word being 0, so in game every wait stayed in
place (60 main loop passes, 30 presents per second). Gate on the cvar only.

Code the render thread runs gets its own state: frame time is the time
between its presents, the timing fixes keep per-thread carries, and the
render node hook and the tick fraction's simulation check only apply on the
main thread. Stats count the presents made by the render thread.
